Z||000000||GT Bastard||04-02-2000||08:04 PM||||I'm curious if anyone knows what differences there are between 84-86, and 87-88 headlight motors and assmeblies.  I know the wiring is different for the 84-86 models, but what about the headlight brackets and assys???||||reg||3
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-02-2000||09:51 PM||||?||||reg||1
Z||000002||cscougar||04-02-2000||10:50 PM||||I installed the 87/88 headlight motors & module in my 85.  The brackets and all are the same.. only change is the module runs the two headlight motors instead of the 3 relays.  <P>I found somewhere on the web a diagram on the wiring and was able to splice the module and headlight motors into the existing wiring.  I removed the old motors and relays and had the fix done in about 1 hour.  The newer style motors are quieter and alot less expensive to repair.  I mounted the module on the wall between the front trunk area and the headlights instead of in the left front fender area.  Have run it this way for 2 years now with no problems.  I have another set ready to mount in my other 85 2m6 as soon as I get time.<P>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-03-2000||07:23 PM||||If you get the harness, which is time consuming but not hard, then this is pretty easy to change. the module uses the 2 control wires from the headlight switch power and ground.||||reg||1
